            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for such a detailed feature request!\r\n\r\nI remember trying to make it work this way but got nowhere because of some technical limitation of how `count` information is provided (for example, `vim.v.count1` only provides multiplication of those two counts, as per `:h v:count`). But if 'vim-sandwich' has it working, I'll look into that.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n> With this structure you also are able to express stuff much more complicated something like `3sa2w([{` would convert `foo bar` to `{[(foo bar)]}`.\r\n\r\nThis, almost certainly, won't be the case. It *will* require much refactoring for only a slight gain of functionality. This particular use case is better resolved with \"user prompt\" `?` surrounding: `sa2w?` followed by `([{<CR>}])<CR>`.",
